---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Support - Ascend"
  description="Get help with your Ascend account, subscription, heart-rate monitor, Apple Health connection, notifications, or account deletion."
>
  <style>
    .support-page {
      min-height: 100vh;
      background:
        radial-gradient(circle at 12% 0%, rgba(134, 211, 10, 0.11), transparent 32%),
        radial-gradient(circle at 100% 24%, #202735 0, var(--bg) 42%);
    }

    .support-page main {
      width: min(100%, 920px);
      margin: 0 auto;
      padding: 132px 24px 72px;
    }

    .eyebrow {
      margin-bottom: 14px;
      color: var(--accent);
      font-size: 13px;
      font-weight: 800;
      letter-spacing: 0.15em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
    }

    .support-page h1 {
      max-width: 720px;
      margin-bottom: 18px;
      font-size: clamp(40px, 6vw, 68px);
      line-height: 1.02;
      letter-spacing: -0.035em;
    }

    .intro {
      max-width: 700px;
      color: #b9c2cf;
      font-size: 18px;
      line-height: 1.65;
    }

    .contact-card {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: 1fr auto;
      align-items: center;
      gap: 24px;
      margin: 40px 0 56px;
      padding: 24px;
      border: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 25%, var(--border));
      border-radius: 16px;
      background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 7%, var(--surface));
    }

    .contact-card h2 {
      margin-bottom: 6px;
      font-size: 21px;
      line-height: 1.25;
    }

    .contact-card p {
      color: var(--muted);
      font-size: 15px;
      line-height: 1.6;
    }

    .contact-button {
      display: inline-flex;
      align-items: center;
      justify-content: center;
      min-height: 48px;
      padding: 12px 18px;
      border: 1px solid var(--accent);
      border-radius: 10px;
      background: var(--accent);
      color: #080c10;
      font-size: 15px;
      font-weight: 800;
      text-decoration: none;
      white-space: nowrap;
      transition: background 0.2s, border-color 0.2s, transform 0.1s;
    }

    .contact-button:hover {
      border-color: var(--accent-hover);
      background: var(--accent-hover);
    }

    .contact-button:active {
      transform: scale(0.98);
    }

    .section-heading {
      margin-bottom: 18px;
      font-size: 24px;
      line-height: 1.2;
    }

    .support-grid {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
      gap: 16px;
    }

    .support-topic {
      padding: 24px;
      border: 1px solid var(--border);
      border-radius: 16px;
      background: rgba(28, 35, 51, 0.86);
    }

    .support-topic h3 {
      margin-bottom: 10px;
      font-size: 19px;
      line-height: 1.3;
    }

    .support-topic p,
    .support-topic li {
      color: var(--muted);
      font-size: 15px;
      line-height: 1.7;
    }

    .support-topic p + p,
    .support-topic ul + p {
      margin-top: 12px;
    }

    .support-topic ul {
      margin: 10px 0 0;
      padding-left: 20px;
    }

    .support-topic li + li {
      margin-top: 7px;
    }

    .support-topic strong {
      color: var(--text);
    }

    .support-page a:not(.contact-button) {
      color: var(--accent);
      text-decoration: none;
    }

    .support-page a:not(.contact-button):hover {
      text-decoration: underline;
    }

    .support-note {
      margin-top: 32px;
      padding: 20px 22px;
      border-left: 3px solid var(--accent);
      border-radius: 0 12px 12px 0;
      background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.035);
      color: var(--muted);
      font-size: 14px;
      line-height: 1.7;
    }

    @media (max-width: 720px) {
      .support-page main {
        padding: 108px 16px 56px;
      }

      .contact-card {
        grid-template-columns: 1fr;
        margin: 32px 0 44px;
      }

      .contact-button {
        width: 100%;
      }

      .support-grid {
        grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      }
    }
  </style>

  <div class="support-page">
    <main>
      <p class="eyebrow">Ascend Support</p>
      <h1>Get back to racing.</h1>
      <p class="intro">
        Fix account access, restore a subscription, reconnect a heart-rate source, or remove your account.
        Start with the steps below, then email us if the problem keeps you off the stair stepper.
      </p>

      <section class="contact-card" aria-labelledby="contact-heading">
        <div>
          <h2 id="contact-heading">Contact Ascend Support</h2>
          <p>
            Email <a href="mailto:pavayt@gmail.com">pavayt@gmail.com</a>.
            Include your device model, iOS version, Ascend app version, and what happened.
            Never send your password.
          </p>
        </div>
        <a
          class="contact-button"
          href="mailto:pavayt@gmail.com?subject=Ascend%20Support"
        >
          Email Support
        </a>
      </section>

      <h2 class="section-heading">Support paths</h2>
      <div class="support-grid">
        <section class="support-topic">
          <h3>Account access</h3>
          <p>
            Sign in with the same Apple or Google account you used to create Ascend.
            Passwords and account recovery stay with that sign-in provider.
          </p>
          <p>
            If the correct provider still does not restore your account, email support with the provider name and the error message.
            Do not send your password or verification code.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="support-topic">
          <h3>Subscription purchase or restore</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>Start a new subscription from Ascend's in-app paywall.</li>
            <li>Restore an existing purchase from the paywall or <strong>Settings &gt; Restore Purchases</strong>.</li>
            <li>Manage or cancel from <strong>Settings &gt; Manage Subscription</strong> in Ascend, which opens your Apple Account subscription settings.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            Deleting Ascend or your Ascend account does not cancel an App Store subscription.
            Apple handles App Store billing and refund requests through <a href="https://reportaproblem.apple.com/">Report a Problem</a>.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="support-topic">
          <h3>Headphones and step counting</h3>
          <p>
            Ascend counts your steps from the motion sensors in your AirPods or Beats.
            An Apple Watch or an iPhone in your pocket cannot count a climb, so a compatible pair is required to race.
          </p>
          <p>
            If Ascend will not start a climb, connect the headphones to this iPhone, wear both sides, and allow Ascend's Motion &amp; Fitness permission in <strong>iOS Settings &gt; Apps &gt; Ascend</strong>.
            The in-app compatible-headphones list shows every supported model.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="support-topic">
          <h3>Heart rate</h3>
          <p>
            For live heart rate and effort zones while you climb, open <strong>Settings &gt; Edit Profile &gt; Integrations &gt; Heart Rate Monitor</strong>.
            Ascend connects to Bluetooth chest straps that use the standard Bluetooth Heart Rate service.
            Turn on Bluetooth, allow Ascend's Bluetooth permission, and disconnect the strap from any other app holding the connection.
          </p>
          <p>
            An Apple Watch cannot stream live heart rate directly to Ascend.
            It can still supply heart rate after the fact: connect Apple Health in <strong>Settings &gt; Edit Profile &gt; Integrations &gt; Apple Health</strong> and allow Ascend to read heart rate, and Ascend attaches what your watch, or any wearable that writes to Apple Health, recorded while you were climbing.
            Ascend does not import workouts from Apple Health.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="support-topic">
          <h3>Notifications</h3>
          <p>
            Open <strong>Settings &gt; Notifications</strong> in Ascend to change climb-drop alerts.
            If iOS permission is off, open <strong>iOS Settings &gt; Apps &gt; Ascend &gt; Notifications</strong> and allow the notification types you want.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="support-topic">
          <h3>Account deletion</h3>
          <p>
            Open <strong>Settings</strong>, scroll to <strong>Delete Account</strong>, and confirm deletion.
            For security, Ascend may ask you to sign in again.
          </p>
          <p>
            If your subscription has lapsed and Ascend is held on the <strong>Open subscription options</strong> screen, use the <strong>Delete account</strong> link below Restore Purchases on that screen.
            Deletion never requires an active subscription.
          </p>
          <p>
            If you cannot access the in-app deletion flow, email <a href="mailto:pavayt@gmail.com?subject=Ascend%20Account%20Deletion">pavayt@gmail.com</a> from the address tied to your account.
            We will verify ownership before acting.
          </p>
        </section>
      </div>

      <p class="support-note">
        Ascend is a racing and fitness app, not a medical service.
        Stop exercising and seek appropriate medical care if you experience pain, dizziness, chest pain, faintness, or another concerning symptom.
      </p>
    </main>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
